    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/math/9210222v1</id>
    <title>Keller's cube-tiling conjecture is false in high dimensions</title>
    <updated>1992-10-01T00:00:00Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/math/9210222v1" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/math/9210222v1" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>  O. H. Keller conjectured in 1930 that in any tiling of $\Bbb R^n$ by unit $n$-cubes there exist two of them having a complete facet in common. O. Perron proved this conjecture for $n\le 6$. We show that for all $n\ge 10$ there exists a tiling of $\Bbb R^n$ by unit $n$-cubes such that no two $n$-cubes have a complete facet in common.</summary>
